# PlotPlanner backend

PlotPlanner is a career-discovery product, built API-first. This repository begins
with the backend because the durable product value is in a user's profile, the
evidence it retrieves, and the actions an agent can take from that evidence.

## Services

| Service | Owns | Public responsibility |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `profile-service` | profiles, interests, goals | stores the user's explicit planning context |
| `knowledge-service` | source documents, chunks, embeddings | ingests and semantically retrieves grounded evidence |
| `agent-service` | agent runs and orchestration policy | composes profile and retrieval tools into planning runs |
| `mcp-server` | MCP tool surface | exposes selected capabilities to MCP-capable clients |

There is deliberately no generic `/api` proxy, chat endpoint, or mock AI response.
Each HTTP endpoint exists to change or retrieve a domain resource. Services own
their data and communicate through typed HTTP contracts; the initial deployment
uses one PostgreSQL cluster with separate schemas, which keeps local operations
simple without sharing tables across services.

## Start locally

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build
```

The compose stack enables the `vector` extension automatically. For development
without containers, install the workspace with `uv sync --all-packages` and run
each service from its directory with `uv run fastapi dev app/main.py`.

## Initial contracts

- `POST /v1/profiles` creates a profile; `GET/PATCH /v1/profiles/{id}` retrieves
  or updates it.
- `POST /v1/documents` accepts a plain-text source and creates its chunks and
  embeddings. `POST /v1/search` retrieves the best matching chunks.
- The agent service has no public run endpoint yet: a run is only useful when an
  authenticated caller and an LLM provider are configured. Its typed tools and
  run model are implemented now so that this capability can be added without
  leaking retrieval logic into an API route.

See [the architecture note](docs/architecture.md) for the service boundaries and
the next implementation increments.
